cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Renascor Atlas: an open database of persons and places tagged by editors in Renaissance-era digital editions"
message: "If you use the Renascor Atlas in your research, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Godbarge
    given-names: Clément
    affiliation: "University of St Andrews"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8699-7582"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Pantagrueliste/renascor-atlas"
url: "https://pantagrueliste.github.io/renascor-atlas/"
abstract: >-
  The Renascor Atlas maps the persons and places tagged by editors in the TEI
  digital editions catalogued by Renascor (1450-1700), with authority-file ids,
  coordinates and mention counts per edition. The underlying texts are
  catalogued in Renascor (DOI 10.5281/zenodo.23345610).
keywords:
  - digital humanities
  - renaissance
  - gazetteer
  - named entities
  - TEI
  - early modern
license: CC0-1.0
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-05
